The report describes two failures: (1) a V02 standardized against its own expanding history, with a regime-dependent sign (unstable across T regimes), and (2) a slow-moving feature (V05 share of positive changes) with high rank autocorrelation of 0.77. The next steps suggested are V02 interacted with T, and faster-moving temporal features.

The proposed expression uses V06 and V04, not V02 or V05. It uses tsz with a 60 window, a rolling time-series z-score, which is not an expanding history, though still a temporal standardization. The hypothesis doesn't address regime dependence (no T interaction), and it doesn't explicitly address slow-moving features. A 60-period rolling z-score spread could be slow-moving too. The hypothesis describes "cross-sectionally standardized" while the expression uses tsz, a mismatch. There is no explicit avoidance of the failures.

{"avoids_failure": false}

